==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|dēterreō||deter, discourage}}, from {{term|lang=la|de||from}} + {{m|la|terreō||I frighten}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/dɪˈtɜː(ɹ)/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-deter.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(r)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|deterr}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[prevent]] something from happening.
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[persuade]] someone not to do something; to [[discourage]].
#* '''1748'''.  David Hume.  ''Enquiries concerning the human understanding and concerning the principles of moral.'' London: Oxford University Press, 1973.  § 10.
#*: we have in following enquiry, attempted to throw some light upon subjects, from which uncertainty has hitherto '''deterred''' the wise

==== Related terms ====
*[[deterrent]]

